Allspice dram, also known as pimento dram, is a liqueur made from the dried berries of the allspice tree (Pimenta dioica). Despite its name, allspice is a single spice, not a blend. The berries have flavors reminiscent of a combination of cinnamon, cloves, and nutmeg, hence the name &quot;allspice.&quot;

To make allspice dram, the dried allspice berries are crushed or ground and then steeped in high-proof alcohol to extract their flavors. This infusion is typically sweetened with sugar, resulting in a sweet and spiced liqueur. The final product often has a warm and aromatic profile, with notes of cinnamon, clove, and nutmeg.

Allspice dram is used as a flavoring agent in cocktails, adding depth and complexity to drinks. It&#039;s a common ingredient in classic and modern tiki cocktails, where its spice-forward profile complements tropical fruit flavors.
